---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RoadmapCard from '@/components/RoadmapCard.astro';
import { roadmap, testing } from '@/data/development';
---
<BaseLayout title="Development · Spirebreak" description="What is changing in Spirebreak right now, what we are testing next, and which parts of the game are still open questions.">
  <section class="page-hero shell">
    <span class="eyebrow">DEVELOPMENT</span>
    <h1>What we are improving next.</h1>
    <p>Spirebreak is already much broader than its first playable build. Mutation V1 and Catalyst Agency now give players stronger transformations and clearer build directions. The current focus is whether those systems create memorable machines players deliberately pursue and want to revisit in another run.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">RIGHT NOW</span>
      <h2>The questions that can still change the game.</h2>
      <p>These are the areas we are actively learning from before we add another large content wave or tune Resonance more aggressively.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid two">{roadmap.filter((item) => item.lane === 'now').map((item) => <RoadmapCard {...item} />)}</div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">PLAYTEST QUESTIONS</span>
      <h2>What we want to see people do naturally.</h2>
      <p>Automated tests can tell us whether the game is stable. They cannot tell us whether someone is already thinking about their next build when a run ends.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="test-grid">{testing.map((item, index) => <article class="test-item"><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><div><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.question}</p></div></article>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell methodology">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">HOW WE WORK</span>
      <h2>Technical confidence first. Player feel second.</h2>
      <p>We keep those two things separate so a green test suite is never mistaken for a fun game.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-grid">
      <article><strong>Build it safely</strong><p>Regression tests protect combat, saves, performance and deterministic systems while the game changes quickly.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Watch real runs</strong><p>Human sessions show whether choices are understandable, builds feel different and difficulty feels fair.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Change what matters</strong><p>We tune the parts players actually struggle with instead of adding more systems just because we can.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
